{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>And it came to pass, because they feared.</b> Because they did not fear the king of Egypt but feared only HaShem, and He dealt well with them. Know that this word is neither among the intransitive verbs nor among the transitive ones, for it follows the pattern whereby a person receives fear from another; therefore, 'they feared HaShem' is the correct interpretation. They took a shorter route, saying 'he feared HaShem' (1 Kings 18:12). Therefore the word נורא is not in the nif'al binyan like נולד (1 Chronicles 2:3), נשבר and נדכה (Psalms 51:19), and the discerning will understand."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:30:51.064483688Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}